{{!
    @template tool_vae/organisation_page

    The page of the organisation under its heading: the link "Help" of the tab, the tabs, the error of the core when the
    competencies are switched off, the pieces of the tab that is open, and the buttons of "My pathway".

    Every text comes from the context, drawn by tool_vae\output\organisation_page. The template holds no logic beyond its
    sections. Every key is HTML, placed as it is (triple braces): guidehtml, drawn by tool_vae/organisation_guide_link (or
    empty); tabshtml, the tabs of the core; noticehtml, a notification of the core (or empty); parthtml, a piece drawn by its
    template (tool_vae/next_actions, organisation_notice, organisation_pathway, organisation_followed, organisation_site,
    scope_box); buttonhtml, a button of the core.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * guidehtml - string, HTML: the link "Help", or empty
    * tabshtml - string, HTML: the tabs
    * noticehtml - string, HTML: the error of the core, or empty
    * parts - array, each {parthtml}: the pieces of the tab, in their order
    * buttons - array, each {buttonhtml}: the buttons offered, in their order

    Example context (json):
    {
        "guidehtml": "<p class=\"tool-vae-guide-link\"><a href=\"https://example.com/admin/tool/vae/guide.php\">Help</a></p>",
        "tabshtml": "<ul class=\"nav nav-tabs\"><li class=\"nav-item\">My pathway</li></ul>",
        "noticehtml": "",
        "parts": [{"parthtml": "<div class=\"alert alert-info\">The panel alone decides.</div>"}],
        "buttons": [{"buttonhtml": "<div class=\"singlebutton\"><button type=\"button\">Declare</button></div>"}]
    }
}}
{{{guidehtml}}}{{{tabshtml}}}{{{noticehtml}}}{{#parts}}{{{parthtml}}}{{/parts}}{{#buttons}}{{{buttonhtml}}}{{/buttons}}
